      "side": 1,
      "message": "Agree that we can replace `pffft::detail::PFFFT_REAL` with `pffft::TransformType::PFFFT_REAL`. However, `PFFFT_FORWARD` does not seem to have a proper shorthand, so is `PFFFT_Setup`. So for uniformity we can use `pffft::detail` everywhere. In my view, the non-canonical NS name problem is on the pffft\u0027s side. Usually \"implementation detail\" namespaces tend to be made less accessible to external code.",
